Kind: ablation
Issue: #763
Takes out: the cut of a long thread name -- mach_thread_set_name() takes any failure of copyinstr() for an unreadable address again, and refuses a name of sixteen characters or more with KERN_INVALID_ADDRESS, as x86-64 did. pthread_test's thread name kernel asks a 26-character name and wants it cut.
Run: --entry 14 1200 -smp 1
Expect: thread name kernel \(long\): FAIL

diff --git a/uros/src/mach_kernel/kern/syscall_subr.c b/uros/src/mach_kernel/kern/syscall_subr.c
index acca1b30..b69c902e 100644
--- a/uros/src/mach_kernel/kern/syscall_subr.c
+++ b/uros/src/mach_kernel/kern/syscall_subr.c
@@ -773,7 +773,7 @@ mach_thread_set_name(const char *name)
 	 * caller.  copyinstr answers both at once, which is why it is the
 	 * whole fix rather than a stac/clac pair around the old loop.
 	 */
-	if (copyinstr(name, buf, sizeof buf, &got) != 0 && got != sizeof buf)
+	if (copyinstr(name, buf, sizeof buf, &got) != 0)
 		return KERN_INVALID_ADDRESS;
 
